<!--
  Fill in the real vendor-id / product-id of your thermal printer (decimal,
  not hex) after checking it on the tablet/PC actually connected to it:
    Android (rooted/ADB shell):  cat /proc/bus/usb/devices   (or `dumpsys usb`)
    Linux/Mac (PC via USB):      lsusb   ->  ID vvvv:pppp   (hex; convert to decimal)
  See README.md for the exact commands and for the HPRT TP801's known IDs.

  Without vendorId/productId this filter matches nothing — that's fine, the
  app still detects the printer at runtime by USB Printer Class (interfaceClass
  == 7) in UsbThermalPrinterPlugin.findDevice(). This file only controls the
  "open this app automatically when a matching USB device is plugged in" OS
  behavior declared in AndroidManifest.xml; it is not required for the plugin
  itself to find/claim the printer once the app is already open.
-->
<resources>
